      \field{abstract}{At the intersection of machine learning and quantum computing, Quantum Machine Learning ({QML}) has the potential of accelerating data analysis, especially for quantum data, with applications for quantum materials, biochemistry, and high-energy physics. Nevertheless, challenges remain regarding the trainability of {QML} models. Here we review current methods and applications for {QML}. We highlight differences between quantum and classical machine learning, with a focus on quantum neural networks and quantum deep learning. Finally, we discuss opportunities for quantum advantage with {QML}.}
